 ComfyUI uses DynamicVRAM and retains the most recent pipeline in VRAM/system RAM. The complete LTX and H3 stacks cannot remain resident together in 32 GB VRAM and 64 GB RAM, so a model switch can still evict weights. Full renders remain serialized; two simultaneous generations would overcommit VRAM.
 
-Use normal `final` mode for maximum quality. H3 `--fast` uses the installed 8-step Turbo LoRA and trades some quality/motion stability for speed. LTX is already the official distilled 8+3-step pipeline; its `draft` mode gains speed by reducing resolution, so the quality loss is more visible.
+Use normal `final` mode for maximum quality. H3 `--fast` retains the legacy four-step FastH3 renderer. The bot fast commands use `--fast --fast-profile taomate`: the tested three-step TaoMate LoRA, Euler/simple and SLA 25% attention. Saved jobs preserve their renderer profile on resume. LTX is already the official distilled 8+3-step pipeline; its `draft` mode gains speed by reducing resolution, so the quality loss is more visible.
 
 ## Worker supervision and stall recovery
 
